{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Iterator","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The elements returned by this iterator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"appear in the order that the tasks "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"completed","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not in the order that those tasks were added to the task group."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This iterator terminates after all tasks have completed successfully,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or after any task completes by throwing an error."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If a task completes by throwing an error,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it doesn’t return any further task results."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"After iterating over the results of each task,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it’s valid to make a new iterator for the task group,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which you can use to iterate over the results of new tasks you add to the group."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can also make a new iterator to resume iteration"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after a child task throws an error."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["group.addTask { 1 }","group.addTask { throw SomeError }","group.addTask { 2 }","","do {","    \/\/ Assuming the child tasks complete in order, this prints \"1\"","    \/\/ and then throws an error.","